  "notes": "The evaluation requires amazon.Order plus file_system.File/Directory to change, so receipts are obtained via amazon.download_order_receipt (passing download_to_file_path and the file_system access token) rather than by extracting them from Gmail confirmation emails; the email hint is only an alternative way to identify orders. The number of orders is unknown up front: the problem uses three placeholder orders (order-1..3) standing for every order returned by amazon.show_orders (iterate over all pages); at runtime one download step is executed per actual order. amazon.show_orders is modeled as a single listing step (orders-listed) that reveals ids and placement dates; each order's target path is a static mapping to its designated file name yyyy-mm-dd__<order_id>.txt inside ~/bills/amazon_purchases/. file_system.create_directory is called once for the target folder (use recursive=true/allow_if_exists=true if the parent ~/bills does not exist). token-for is a static fact that pins which token object belongs to which app so bindings are unambiguous. supervisor.complete_task takes the (distinct) order records so its precondition mirrors the goal conjunction; it is called without an answer.",
